 "persona_full": "[Who I am]\n- I am a woman.\n- I am 52 years old.\n- I live in Gujarat.\n- The place I live in has under 2,000 inhabitants.\n- I am Hindu.\n- I am widowed.\n- I do not live with my parents.\n- My education: complete primary school.\n- I can read and write.\n\n[Work and money]\n- My work situation: full-time employee.\n- I am not the chief wage earner in my household.\n- I would describe my family as lower middle class.\n- On a ladder of household incomes in India from 1 (lowest) to 10 (highest), my household is at 4.\n- In the past year my family spent some savings.\n- My satisfaction with my household's financial situation, from 1 (completely dissatisfied) to 10 (completely satisfied): 4.\n- In the last 12 months my family has never gone without enough food to eat.\n- In the last 12 months my family has rarely gone without a cash income.\n\n[My life]\n- Taking all things together, I am rather happy.\n- My health these days is good.\n- My satisfaction with my life as a whole, from 1 (completely dissatisfied) to 10 (completely satisfied): 4.\n- How much free choice and control I feel I have over my life, from 1 (none at all) to 10 (a great deal): 5.\n- In my neighbourhood I feel quite secure.\n- Family is very important in my life.\n- Friends are rather important in my life.\n- Work is rather important in my life.\n- Politics is not at all important in my life.\n- Religion is rather important in my life.\n\n[Religion]\n- Apart from weddings and funerals, I attend religious services once a month.\n- How important God is in my life, from 1 (not at all important) to 10 (very important): 9.\n\n[How I see other people]\n- My family: I trust them somewhat.\n- People in my neighbourhood: I trust them somewhat.\n- People of another religion: I trust them somewhat.\n- People of another nationality: I do not trust them very much.\n\n[What kind of person I am]\n- Thinking up new ideas and being creative, doing things my own way: not like me.\n- Being rich, having a lot of money and expensive things: not like me.\n- Living in secure surroundings, avoiding anything that might be dangerous: somewhat like me.\n- Always behaving properly, avoiding anything people would say is wrong: somewhat like me.\n\n[My views]\n- I am not at all interested in politics.\n- From 1 (incomes should be made more equal) to 10 (we need larger income differences as incentives for individual effort), my view is 1.\n- Cheating on taxes if you have a chance, from 1 (never justifiable) to 10 (always justifiable): 1.\n- I am quite proud to be Indian.\n\n[How I get information]\n- How often I read a daily newspaper: daily.\n- How often I watch TV news: daily.\n- How often I use the internet: less than monthly.",
